<title>UK: Euromarket turnover data for 31 Oct revised -ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover data for 31 Oct revised -ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in Eurobond and related markets fell to $971.3 billion in the week to October 31 from $997.1 billion the previous week, International Securities Market Association data showed.</p>
<p>This is a revision of data given last week which said turnover for the week to Oct 31 was $980.8 billion, ISMA said in a statement on Monday. Primary market figures and the amount cleared through Cedel were revised.</p>
<p>(in billions of dollars):</p>
<p>					  Latest week	Previous week</p>
<p> Primary market:		     48.60		54.13</p>
<p> Of which U.S. dollar issues     26.49		26.56</p>
<p> Secondary market:		  922.70	     942.97</p>
<p> Of which U.S. dollar issues    183.20	     177.22</p>
<p> Cleared through Euroclear	690.56	     715.17</p>
<p> Cleared through Cedel	    280.74	     281.93</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
